(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase463AslFirstBeyondRacket"
  :createdAt 1789260000000
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 4
  :summary "ASL-First Beyond Racket: lead on the axes Racket never optimised, being emission reliability, nesting depth, binding distance and a measured error rate, after measurement closed the structural rewrite that looked like the largest win."
  :phase "Phase463AslFirstBeyondRacket"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-12 under cl100k over 888 files and 1512691 tokens. Structural delimiters are 12.66 percent of the corpus, 121331 tokens opening and 70147 closing, the third largest category after string literals at 41.8 percent and identifiers at 20.4 percent. Nesting reaches depth 32, 13.4 percent of openings are deeper than 8, and the modal depth is 5. Closing runs are already merged by the tokenizer into single tokens at lengths one through five. Two structural rewrites were measured and both failed: deleting delimiters from the existing formatting appeared to save 13.6 percent but produces an unparseable file and measures nothing, and a real indentation-significant rendering that preserves the tree costs 7.7 percent more, because every level pays a newline and an indent while a paren run pays one token. Making trailing closers implicit saves 0.39 percent. S-expressions with explicit delimiters are therefore the token-optimal structural encoding at this corpus depth, and the structural tax is not overhead to remove."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task46301"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-463"
      :title "Nesting depth is a bounded, tracked quantity"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "emission"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789260000000
      :updatedAt 1789429800000
      :motivation "Depth is the quantity a generating model has to carry in working state, and it is unbounded here: 32 at the maximum and deeper than 8 in 13.4 percent of openings. A closing run of four is one token to read and four decisions to emit, and a single miscount invalidates the whole file. Racket answers this with editor tooling for a human; there is no human here. Depth is measurable, it is under our control, and nobody has ever tracked it."
      :purpose "Depth is reported per file and per form in the inventory, a declared ceiling applies, and a form exceeding it is a finding naming the form rather than a style note. The ceiling is chosen from the measured distribution rather than asserted, and lowering it over time is tracked like any other ratchet."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Depth reported per file and per form" "A ceiling derived from the measured distribution" "Exceeding forms named individually" "Depth added to the tracked inventory"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols ["check_file_delimiters"]
      :relatedSymbols ["bounded" "output" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45704"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46301"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46301.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A form nested one level past the ceiling is reported with its path and line." "Depth inside a string literal is not counted." "The reported distribution is recomputed from the tree, not read from a record."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46301" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define nestingDepthCeilingRule semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46301-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Compute the distribution." "Choose the ceiling from it." "Report exceeding forms." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task46301-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46302"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-463"
      :title "Flattening forms, adopted only on a measured double win"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "emission"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789260000000
      :updatedAt 1789430200000
      :motivation "The way to reduce depth is not to remove delimiters, which was measured and costs 7.7 percent, but to stop nesting in the first place. A chain of transformations written as nested applications reaches depth quickly and reads back to front; the same chain written as a sequence is flat. The corpus has a modal depth of 5 with a long tail, and most of that tail is chained calls and nested let bindings rather than genuine structure."
      :purpose "A small set of flattening forms is introduced, each admitted only when it lowers both the measured depth and the measured token count on real corpus sites. A form that lowers depth while raising tokens, or the reverse, is recorded as rejected with both numbers. No form is adopted on the grounds that it reads better."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Flattening forms admitted on a measured double win" "Rejected candidates recorded with both numbers" "Depth tail reduced measurably rather than stylistically"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn" "asl/tools/engine_js.h"]
      :targetSymbols ["let"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "semantics" "output"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46301" "Task46102"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46302"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46302.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Rewriting a real corpus site with the form lowers both measured quantities, and the case quotes both before and after." "A candidate that lowers only one is rejected by the gate, not by judgement." "The flattened form and the nested form evaluate identically on the same inputs."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46302" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define flatteningFormDoubleWinRule semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46302-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Find the depth tail sites." "Propose forms." "Measure both quantities per candidate." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task46302-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46303"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-463"
      :title "A binding is never far from its use"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "attention"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789260000000
      :updatedAt 1789430500000
      :motivation "Every retrieval path in this project delivers a slice of a file, and a slice that contains a use without its binding is uninterpretable. Measured, the median distance from an alias declaration to its use is 53 lines, the ninetieth percentile is 232 and the maximum is 1172, with 11.7 percent of 11132 uses beyond 200 lines. Racket has no notion of this quantity because it assumes a reader who can navigate. The consumer here cannot navigate; it receives a window."
      :purpose "Distance between a binding and its uses is measured and bounded. Where the bound cannot be met the binding is made self describing instead, so the slice carries its own meaning, and the choice between moving the binding and making it self describing is recorded per site."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Binding to use distance measured and bounded" "Self describing bindings where distance is unavoidable" "A slice interpretable without the rest of its file"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/packages" "harness/src"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["context" "bounded" "output"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45904"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46303"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46303.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A use beyond the bound whose binding is not self describing is reported with both line numbers." "A slice taken around any use resolves every symbol it contains." "The measurement runs over the resolved graph, so a distance created through re-export is counted."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46303" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define bindingToUseDistanceRule semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46303-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Measure distances over the resolved graph." "Bound them." "Move or make self describing per site." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task46303-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46304"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-463"
      :title "A measured emission error rate, which no language has"
      :kind :verification
      :state :completed
      :lane "emission"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789260000000
      :updatedAt 1789430800000
      :motivation "Every claim about a language being better for models finally rests on whether a model produces correct output in it, and that quantity has never been measured here or anywhere for this language. Token counts, symbol surface and nesting depth are all proxies for it. Without it, a design argument between two forms cannot be settled except by opinion, and this session has already shown how much opinion about token economy turns out to be wrong when measured."
      :purpose "A fixed task set is generated in the language by several models, and the outcome is measured as the rate of forms that fail to parse, fail to bind, or fail their own assertions. The rate is recorded per model and per language variant, so a proposed change is evaluated by generating against it rather than by argument, and a change that lowers tokens while raising the error rate is rejected."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["An emission error rate per model and per variant" "Language changes decided by generation, not argument" "A token saving that raises the error rate rejected" "The proxies calibrated against the quantity they proxy for"]
      :owns ["asl/bench" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "gates" "grading"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46301" "Task45905"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46304"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46304.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Two language variants differing in one form produce two different measured rates on the same task set." "A variant lowering tokens and raising the rate is rejected by the gate." "The task set is fixed and versioned, so a rate is comparable across dates."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46304" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define measuredEmissionErrorRateRule semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46304-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Fix and version the task set." "Generate across models and variants." "Record rates." "Bind language decisions to them." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task46304-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46305"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-463"
      :title "Record the refuted rewrites so they do not return"
      :kind :protocol
      :state :planned
      :lane "emission"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789260000000
      :updatedAt 1789260000000
      :motivation "Three structural compaction ideas were measured in one session and all three failed: devowelling raises cost by 106 percent, deleting delimiters from existing formatting appears to save 13.6 percent while producing an unparseable file, and a real indentation-significant rendering costs 7.7 percent more because each level pays a newline and an indent. Each of the three is intuitive, each will be proposed again, and each is cheap to re-measure and expensive to half-adopt."
      :purpose "The refuted rewrites are recorded with their measurements, their method and the reason the intuition fails, alongside the surviving conclusion that explicit delimiters are the token-optimal encoding at this corpus depth. A proposal to reopen one carries a new measurement rather than a fresh argument."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Three refutations recorded with method and number" "The surviving conclusion recorded with its scope" "Reopening requires measurement"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/principles.asn" "TOKEN_CONVENTIONS.md"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46201"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46305"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46305.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Each recorded refutation is reproducible by command on the current tree." "A recorded number that no longer reproduces fails the check rather than standing." "The record names the scope, so a conclusion true at this depth is not read as universal."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46305" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Record the three refutations." "Make each reproducible by command." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])]
  :notes "The largest apparent win in this session was structural and it did not survive its own measurement. What remains as genuinely ASL-first is the set of quantities no existing language tracks: nesting depth as an emission cost, distance from a binding to its use as an attention cost, and above all a measured emission error rate, which converts every future language argument from opinion into a comparison.")
